    <preface>
      <p><b>STATES </b><b>GRANTS (HOME CARE) AMENDMENT ACT 1978</b></p>
      <p><b>No. 113</b><b> </b><b>of 1978</b></p>
      <p>An Act to amend the <i>States Grants (Home Care) Act </i>1969.</p>
      <p>BE IT ENACTED by the Queen, and the Senate and House of Representatives of the Commonwealth of Australia, as follows:</p>
      <p><b>Short title, &amp;c.</b></p>
    </preface>
    <body>
      <section eId="sec-1">
        <num>1</num>
        <subsection eId="sec-1__subsec-1">
          <num>1</num>
          <content>
            <p><b>1. </b>(1) This Act may be cited as the <i>States Grants (Home Care) Amendment Act </i>1978.</p>
          </content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec-1__subsec-2">
          <num>2</num>
          <content>
            <p>(2) The <i>States Grants (Home Care) Act </i>1969 is in this Act referred to as the Principal Act.</p>
          </content>
        </subsection>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec-2">
        <num>2</num>
        <heading>Commencement</heading>
        <content>
          <p><b>2.</b> This Act shall come into operation on the day on which it receives the Royal Assent.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec-3">
        <num>3</num>
        <heading>Grant of financial assistance in connexion with home care services</heading>
        <content>
          <p><b>3.</b> Section 6 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting from sub-section (1) “two-thirds” and substituting “one-half”.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec-4">
        <num>4</num>
        <heading>Grant of financial assistance in respect of salaries</heading>
        <content>
          <p><b>4.</b> Section 10 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting from sub-section (1) “two-thirds” and substituting “one-half”.</p>
          <p><b>Application </b><b>of </b><b>amendments</b></p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec-5">
        <num>5</num>
        <subsection eId="sec-5__subsec-1">
          <num>1</num>
          <content>
            <p><b>5.</b> (1) The amendment made by <ref href="#sec-3">section 3</ref> has effect in relation to the year that commenced on 1 July 1978 and subsequent years.</p>
          </content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec-5__subsec-2">
          <num>2</num>
          <content>
            <p>The amendment made by <ref href="#sec-4">section 4</ref> has effect in relation to salary paid in respect of any period that commenced on or after <date date="1978-07-01">1 July 1978</date>.</p>
          </content>
        </subsection>
      </section>
